#
# Read this before adding a line. A fingerprint is `<commit>:<path>:<ruleID>:<line>` and is
# pinned to ONE line of ONE blob in ONE commit, so an entry here cannot suppress a future
# finding — not even a real secret on the next line of the same file. That is the only form
# an entry may take: never a path glob, never a bare rule name, never a regex allowlist.
#
